gametitle=Ace Combat 5: The Unsung War [SLUS-20851] (NTSC-U)

// Target display: 3840x1600, whose aspect ratio is 3840/1600 = 2.4:1.

[True 2.4:1 - 3840x1600]
author=danyole7
description=Corrects 3D projection and vertical FOV for a 2.4:1 display; subtitle correction included. HUD remains stretched. Includes scripted cutscene Hor+ correction. Fully restart the game after updating.

// SPECIAL THANKS:
// nemesis2000's corrected 16:9 projection was the baseline. To preserve object
// proportions when that image fills a 3840x1600 display, the horizontal
// projection scale must be reduced in inverse proportion to the wider image:
// (16/9) / (3840/1600) = (16/9) / 2.4 = 20/27 = 0.7407407.
// A smaller projection scale widens the horizontal field instead of stretching
// the existing 16:9 picture across the extra monitor width.

// f03 camera projection value: 317.36694 (float 0x439EAEF8).
// Loaded at 0x0015CD08 from 0x00440828, then copied to the runtime
// camera fields at offsets 0x10C and 0x114 for the view modes using f03.
// Calculation for our 3840x1600 target:
// 428.44492 (the corrected 16:9 f03 value) * 20/27 = approximately
// 317.3666. The retained tested value 0x439EAEF8 is 317.366943359375;
// it is close to, but not the exact nearest-float rounding of, that result.
patch=1,EE,00440828,word,439EAEF8

// f04 camera projection value: 348.81665 (float 0x43AE6888).
// Loaded at 0x0015CD10 from 0x0044082C and copied to runtime offset 0x110.
// The active aircraft camera selected this path when its mode byte was 1.
// Both the old 16:9 and published 21:9 patches used 0x43EB7385 here,
// leaving this camera at its 16:9 projection and stretching the aircraft.
// Calculation for our 3840x1600 target:
// 470.90250 (the corrected 16:9 f04 value) * 20/27 = 348.81665,
// encoded as float 0x43AE6888. Scaling f04 was the missing correction
// that fixed the aircraft proportions in the active camera mode.
patch=1,EE,0044082C,word,43AE6888

// Virtual vertical dimension: 270.0 (float 0x43870000).
// Executable inspection places this at main object +0x3FF0 +0x04.
// Setter 0x00320710 stores the second dimension here at instruction 0x00320724.
// Update code loads it at 0x003208A0 and divides an output vertical dimension
// by it at 0x003208B8, producing a derived scale at structure offset +0x19C.
// This is a projection/screen-scaling dimension, NOT an angle of 270 degrees.
// Unlike the first two values, 270.0 originally came from the published
// ultrawide patch, not our 20/27 calculation. It was retained after the
// successful gameplay test. Our older 16:9 save contains 360.0 here.
// The visible result depends on derived/cached values: restart the mission
// after changing it. A raw patch write does not execute the setter or mark
// its dirty flag, and a mid-mission reload alone may have no immediate effect.
patch=1,EE,005CC624,word,43870000

// Subtitle correction only.
// Retains the existing dialogue/radio-caption routines and their shared parser.
// v4_dialogue
